-- examples/checks/agg-incr-twice.rofl — agg_incr_twice: A CELL THE FACT SUPPORTS
-- THAT A RULE READ AGAIN WHOLE OWNS. A rule that reads the retracted relation
-- outside its aggregate as well as inside it is read again whole (its facts and
-- cells gone, the rule fired again), so its own cell is not subtracted from: a
-- cell subtracted first would be a count of nothing for a group that has no sale
-- left, which a fresh evaluation does not hold (the rule has no group to ask).
--
--   tw_sale(1, b, 5)   b has no sale left: tw_twice(b, 1) goes, and its cell with it
edb(tw_sale).
tw_sale(1, b, 5).
tw_sale(2, a, 3).
tw_sale(3, a, 4).
tw_twice(G, N) :- tw_sale(_, G, _), N is count(K : tw_sale(K, G, _)).

-- the state after the retraction, row by row
-- expect-row: tw_twice[main](a,2) tick drv support=2
-- and nothing of what it supported before
-- expect-no-row: tw_twice[main](b,
-- expect-no-row: agg_cell[$kernel]($cell(rc82b8553,2,0,$cons(b,
-- expect-no-row: cell $cell(rc82b8553,2,0,$cons(b,
